# HW-019 attempt 1 - 2026-07-12, StickS3 on COM35 (ESP32-S3-PICO-1-N8R8,
# MAC 98:88:e0:0e:dc:64, a THIRD physical device: independent of the boards used
# for HW-006/HW-016 and HW-018). Image: hw019-sweep-7391bbc.bin, built from 7391bbc.
#
# VERDICT: the sweep FAILED, and the fault is in the TEST, not the codec.
#
# sweep_one() raised the amplifier and then k_msleep(AMP_SETTLE_MS = 20) with the
# full-duplex stream running: nobody feeding TX, nobody draining RX. Both halves of
# that bill came due, and both are predicted to the decimal from AMP_SETTLE_MS,
# BLOCK_FRAMES (256) and the 2-block pre-queue, with nothing fitted:
#
#   * RX queues blocks nobody reads, so the timed loop finishes in fewer than 40
#     block-times and the measured frame clock comes out HIGH in exact proportion
#     to the rate.  predicted / observed:
#         8000  +1.59% / +1.68%      16000 +3.23% / +3.41%
#        11025  +2.20% / +2.33%      22050 +4.50% / +4.78%
#        12000  +2.40% / +2.54%      24000 +4.92% / +5.21%
#     (2% tolerance, so everything above 8 kHz was failed by the measurement.)
#
#   * TX runs dry. Two pre-queued blocks hold 2 * 256 / rate seconds of audio, which
#     falls under the 20 ms settle at 32 kHz. Predicted to underrun into I2S ERROR
#     (-EIO) at 32000, 44100 and 48000 and at no lower rate. Observed: exactly those
#     three, and no others.
#
# THE CONTROL IS IN THIS LOG. The restore measurement runs the same code with no
# sleep in it, and read `lrck measured 16000 Hz, want 16000  OK` -- on this board,
# through this driver, at a rate the per-rate loop had just called BAD (16546).
#
# WHAT THIS RUN DOES ESTABLISH, on silicon:
#   * regs=OK at all NINE rates: the identical clock-register set the 256fs argument
#     rests on is written and reads back at every rate from 8 kHz to 48 kHz.
#   * ALL THREE ROUTE TRANSITIONS PASS: playback-only, capture-only and both, with
#     0x01/0x09/0x0A/0x0D/0x0E/0x12/0x14 read back off the real chip. Those values
#     had never touched silicon before this run.
#   * adc=alive from 8 kHz to 24 kHz: the codec's clock tree locks and the modulator
#     runs. (32 kHz and up died before their line was printed -- a second test flaw,
#     now fixed: the diagnostic line is printed even when a phase errors.)
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT ESTABLISH: the frame clock at 11025 Hz and above. That measurement
# was invalid. HW-019b re-runs it with the settle draining the stream instead of
# sleeping in it.
#
